  <text xml:base="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.apokoptomenos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><body n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.apokoptomenos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc"><div type="edition" n="urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0402.apokoptomenos.meineke1840-grc1" xml:lang="grc" corresp="urn:cite2:perseus:fragmentaryplays.v1:tlg0402_apokoptomenos"><head>ΑΠΟΚΟΠΤΟΜΕΝΟΣ</head><div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1">
              <head>I.</head>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1-l1">Λέγεται γὰρ λόγος</l>
                <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1-l2">ὑπὸ τῶν σοφιστῶν, μὴ πέτεσθαι τὸν θεόν</l>
              </lg>
              <pb n="393" facs="urn:hathi:hvd.32044079388682:scan:401" />
              <lg>
                <l n="3" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1-l3">τὸν Ἔρωτα, τοὺς δ᾽ ἐρῶντας· αἰτίαν δ᾽ ἔχειν</l>
                <l n="4" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1-l4">ἐκεῖνον ἄλλως, ἠγνοηκότας δὲ τοὺς</l>
                <l n="5" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1-l5">γραφεῖς ἔχοντα πτέρυγας αὐτὸν ζωγραφεῖν.</l>
              </lg>
              <note type="source">
                <bibl>Athenaeus XIII p. 562 d.</bibl> de Amoris vi et natura agens: <quote>῎Αλεξις δ᾽ ἐν Ἀποκοπτομένῳ <title>Λέγεται γὰρ λόγος</title> κτλ.</quote>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Respicit locum Eustathius p. 987 25. Vs. 1 <quote>λέγεται λόγος</quote>, ut apud Phrynichum Hephaest. p. 67: <quote>λόγος ὥσπερ λέγεται</quote>. Quam locutionem minus graecam esse dicebat Bernhardius noster Eratosth. p. 110.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="2" ana="#compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-2">
              <head>II.</head>
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-2-l1">Οὐ συμποσίαρχος ἦν γὰρ ἀλλὰ δήμιος</l>
                <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-2-l2">ὁ Χαιρέας, κυάθους τροπίνων εἴκοσιν.</l>
              </lg>
              <note type="source">
                <bibl>Athenaeus X p. 431 c:</bibl>
                <quote>῎Αλεξις δ᾽ ἐν Ἀποκοπτομένῳ <title>Οὐ συμποσίαρχος</title> κτλ.</quote>
              </note>
              <note type="apparatus">Quae his addita leguntur in libris <quote>ἴσον ἴσῳ πάλιν τὴν μείζονα ᾔτουν</quote>, ea ex Sophili loco p. 431 a. temere esse repetita, docuerunt Schweighaeuserus et Porsonus.</note>
            </div>
            <div type="textpart" subtype="fragment" n="1_2" ana="#compiled-duplicate-number #compiled-citation-normalized" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2">
              <lg>
                <l n="1" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2-l1">Fertur haec sententia</l>
                <l n="2" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2-l2">inter sapientes, non volare Cupidinem,</l>
                <l n="3" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2-l3">sed eos qui cupiunt. illum onerari crimine</l>
                <l n="4" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2-l4">alieno, perque pictorum ignorantiam</l>
                <l n="5" xml:id="meineke-0402-apokoptomenos-1_2-l5">adstare passim cum pennigero corpore.</l>
              </lg>
            </div>
          </div></body></text></TEI>